{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md; sed -n '221,440p' Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md; sed -n '441,700p' Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md; sed -n '221,440p' Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md; sed -n '441,700p' Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md\"","aggregated_output":"# No Safe Circle — Autonomous AI Development Pipeline\r\n\r\n## Master Context / Architecture Handoff\r\n\r\nUse this file for the durable target architecture when continuing work on the autonomous development pipeline.\r\n\r\nFor exact current implementation status, always read `CURRENT_STATE.md` first.\r\n\r\nLast architecture/status reconciliation: 2026-08-21, after Milestone 1 completion and the post-M1 adversarial-architecture-review branch merge.\r\n\r\n## Current Architecture Status\r\n\r\nThe architecture is no longer purely prospective.\r\n\r\n**Milestone 1 is implemented and merged.** The repository now contains:\r\n\r\n- a human-approved persistent work graph under `Tasks/`;\r\n- stable `NSC-###` work IDs;\r\n- reconciliation-key provenance;\r\n- deterministic graph validation;\r\n- deterministic dependency/parent hierarchy reconstruction;\r\n- exclusive-resource metadata;\r\n- project-level non-code requirements;\r\n- a working local `taskcontrol` CLI;\r\n- a real deterministic ready frontier.\r\n\r\nThe current graph contains 37 work records and the first real `taskcontrol ready` calculation returned seven executable one-agent implementation tasks.\r\n\r\nThe next planned infrastructure milestone is Milestone 2: targeted GDD/project context, Progressive Decomposition, and Artifact Authority.\r\n\r\nBefore substantial Milestone 2 expansion, the M1-complete architecture should be reviewed through `Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/` and any accepted architectural corrections should be persisted in `DECISIONS.md` and `CURRENT_STATE.md`.\r\n\r\n## Project\r\n\r\nRepository: `https://github.com/cathode26/NoSafeCircle`\r\n\r\nCourse work already provides reusable building blocks:\r\n\r\n- Assignment 3: Agent Crew concept — Planner → Implementer → Validator.\r\n- Assignment 4: RAG/retrieval over the No Safe Circle GDD.\r\n- Assignment 5: goal-oriented gap analysis and bounded implementation agent.\r\n- Assignment 6: working GER implementation — Implement/Generate → Evaluate → Refine → Circuit Breaker, including runtime-feedback repair.\r\n- Assignment 7: not yet implemented; intended to become a scored Style Evaluator specialization when real authorized style-sensitive artifact work exists.\r\n\r\nThe production goal is to evolve these pieces into a system that can continue developing No Safe Circle while keeping project state durable, observable, resumable after model/context failures, bounded in cost, grounded in real Unity evidence, and protected from silent AI invention of missing game design.\r\n\r\n## Core Architectural Decision\r\n\r\nThe LLM does **not** own durable project state or the continuous autonomous loop.\r\n\r\nA local deterministic supervisor eventually owns the loop.\r\n\r\nClaude or another coding model is a bounded worker that receives one small piece of approved work at a time.\r\n\r\nPersistent project state lives in repository artifacts and later GitHub operational state, not in a model context window.\r\n\r\nA worker may implement or generate work, but it does not declare that work complete. Completion is determined by project evidence plus merge/approval state.\r\n\r\nAn implementation worker also does not silently invent missing game design. Missing design becomes an explicit artifact proposal.\r\n\r\n## Desired End-to-End Loop\r\n\r\n```text\r\nGDD / Root Canon\r\n ↓\r\nPersistent Work Graph                         ← M1 COMPLETE\r\n ↓\r\nReady / Near-Ready Frontier                   ← M1 COMPLETE\r\n ↓\r\nTargeted Task + GDD + Project Context          ← M2 NEXT\r\n ↓\r\nProgressive Decomposer\r\n ↓\r\nEnough approved information?\r\n ├─ yes → Concrete child work\r\n └─ no  → Proposed artifact\r\n               ↓\r\n         Artifact Authority Gate\r\n               ↓\r\n          Authorized?\r\n          /       \\\r\n        yes        no\r\n         ↓          ↓\r\n   Artifact Generator   Re-plan / Human Review\r\n         ↓\r\n      Artifact GER\r\n         ├─ Canon / Design Evaluator\r\n         ├─ Completeness Evaluator\r\n         └─ Style Evaluator when applicable\r\n         ↓\r\n   Approved Artifact\r\n         ↓\r\n   Back to Decomposer\r\n         ↓\r\n   Concrete Work Item\r\n         ↓\r\nLocal Supervisor                               ← M3\r\n ↓\r\nClaim Ticket\r\n ↓\r\nGit Branch + Git Worktree + Draft PR\r\n ↓\r\nBuild Small Context Package\r\n ↓\r\nBounded Worker / Agent Crew\r\n ↓\r\n==============================\r\n        GER EXECUTION LOOP                     ← M4 production integration\r\n------------------------------\r\nImplement / Generate\r\n ↓\r\nTask/GDD/Artifact Evaluation\r\n ↓\r\nDeterministic Validation\r\n ↓\r\nUnity / Runtime Validation\r\n ↓\r\nPASS?\r\n ├─ yes → Approved Work\r\n └─ no  → Feedback Bundle → Refiner → Re-evaluate\r\n                         ↓\r\n                 retry/cost/runtime limit\r\n                         ↓\r\n                  Circuit Breaker\r\n==============================\r\n ↓\r\nFresh AI Diff Review\r\n ↓\r\nPR Merge / Artifact Approval\r\n ↓\r\nWork = Complete\r\n ↓\r\nDependency Graph Recalculates\r\n ↓\r\nNew Work Becomes Ready\r\n ↓\r\nContinuous Safe Backlog Processing             ← M5\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe exact evaluator order may vary by work type, but cheap deterministic failures should be detected before spending model tokens on semantic review whenever practical.\r\n\r\n## Guiding Principle\r\n\r\n**Use deterministic code for facts and computation. Use LLMs for semantic judgment and bounded implementation.**\r\n\r\nDeterministic/local responsibilities include:\r\n\r\n- work identity and dependency bookkeeping;\r\n- graph validation/readiness;\r\n- file enumeration;\r\n- code/component detection;\r\n- Unity YAML inspection;\r\n- `.meta` GUID relationships;\r\n- obvious project-state queries;\r\n- Git/scope checks;\r\n- compilation/test orchestration;\r\n- progress/no-op detection;\r\n- budget/circuit-breaker bookkeeping.\r\n\r\nLLM responsibilities include:\r\n\r\n- semantic decomposition of bounded near-frontier work;\r\n- deciding whether approved information is sufficient to decompose;\r\n- distinguishing missing design from oversized implementation scope;\r\n- interpreting genuinely ambiguous intent;\r\n- bounded implementation planning/coding;\r\n- semantic task/GDD evaluation;\r\n- fresh semantic diff review;\r\n- authorized design/content generation;\r\n- style evaluation/refinement;\r\n- repair from structured failure evidence.\r\n\r\n## Sources of Truth\r\n\r\n### Root Canon\r\n\r\nThe current GDD is root game-design canon.\r\n\r\nRAG should retrieve only relevant canonical chunks instead of repeatedly sending the entire GDD to a model.\r\n\r\nPrior assignment artifacts may provide history or reusable machinery, but they do not override current GDD or integrated repository state.\r\n\r\n### Approved Design Extensions\r\n\r\nApproved artifact outputs may later extend root canon with project-authorized detail.\r\n\r\nAn artifact becomes trusted only after this path:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nArtifact proposal\r\n ↓\r\nArtifact Authority Gate\r\n ↓\r\nAuthorized generation\r\n ↓\r\nRequired evaluators / GER\r\n ↓\r\nApproved artifact\r\n ↓\r\nTrusted downstream input\r\n```\r\n\r\nApproved artifacts may add detail only inside the authority granted to them. They may not contradict or silently replace GDD canon.\r\n\r\nUnapproved drafts are not trusted design input.\r\n\r\n### Codebase Truth\r\n\r\nThe current integrated `main` branch is the authority for what implementation actually exists and is complete.\r\n\r\nOld assignment planning output is not current codebase truth unless reconciled against the repository.\r\n\r\n### Durable Work Definition\r\n\r\nThe living operational work graph now exists under:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nTasks/\r\n  NSC-001.yaml\r\n  ...\r\n  NSC-037.yaml\r\n```\r\n\r\nInitial supported work kinds are:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nfeature\r\nartifact\r\nimplementation\r\n```\r\n\r\nDefinitions:\r\n\r\n- `feature` — organizational/high-level work that may require progressive decomposition; never a direct implementation handoff.\r\n- `artifact` — work whose output is approved design/content; complete only after required authority/evaluation/promotion.\r\n- `implementation` — concrete repository work that can be executed when dependencies and execution scope allow it.\r\n\r\nStable `reconciliation_key` values preserve traceability back to the reconciliation record that proposed each initial work item.\r\n\r\n### Operational Status\r\n\r\nDurable task definitions currently use `open` / `complete`.\r\n\r\nLater, GitHub Issues/Projects should provide human-facing transient execution visibility such as:\r\n\r\n- Backlog\r\n- Ready\r\n- In Progress\r\n- Blocked\r\n- Validating\r\n- Needs Review\r\n- Done\r\n\r\nDo not make ephemeral “worker is running” state a constantly committed task-file concern if the supervisor/GitHub can own it safely.\r\n\r\n## Milestone 1 Persistent Work Graph\r\n\r\nMilestone 1 is complete. See `01_MILESTONE_TASK_GRAPH.md` for its completion record.\r\n\r\nThe initial graph was created through:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nGDD + repository state\r\n ↓\r\nimmutable reconciliation snapshot\r\n ↓\r\nindependent multi-model verification\r\n ↓\r\nbounded repair / re-verification\r\n ↓\r\n0 final material findings\r\n ↓\r\nhuman approval\r\n ↓\r\ndeterministic bootstrap\r\n ↓\r\npersistent graph\r\n```\r\n\r\nApproved reconciliation:\r\n\r\n`20260821T193541Z-998ee7b5`\r\n\r\nSuccessful verification:\r\n\r\n`20260821T195959Z-43dba5de`\r\n\r\nThe one-time bootstrap is marked by:\r\n\r\n`Pipeline/TaskGraph/BOOTSTRAP_PERSISTED.json`\r\n\r\nDo not rerun the initial `--apply` bootstrap after that marker exists.\r\n\r\n### Current Task-Control Interface\r\n\r\n```text\r\npython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py validate\r\npython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py list\r\npython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py show NSC-003\r\npython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py ready\r\npython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py graph\r\n```\r\n\r\nA work item is executable-ready only when it is open, is an `artifact` or `implementation`, has `execution_scope: single_agent`, and all dependencies are complete.\r\n\r\nThis readiness calculation is deterministic.\r\n\r\n## Reconciliation Boundary\r\n\r\nReconciliation is an immutable point-in-time observation, not the mutable work database.\r\n\r\nEvery full reconciliation run creates a new versioned snapshot of GDD requirements versus repository state.\r\n\r\nA later reconciliation may propose additions/changes/conflicts against the persistent graph, but the Reconciliation Agent does not directly rewrite `Tasks/*.yaml`.\r\n\r\nFuture graph changes must cross an explicit deterministic diff/review/apply boundary.\r\n\r\nOld reconciliation snapshots remain historically true even after later implementation changes the repository.\r\n\r\nThe persistent graph is the living operational state.\r\n\r\n## Progressive Task Decomposition\r\n\r\nThe graph should **not** contain the entire game's lowest-level implementation plan in advance.\r\n\r\nHigh-level work is decomposed just in time as it approaches the actionable frontier.\r\n\r\nThe Progressive Decomposer must first determine *why* an item is not a safe one-agent handoff.\r\n\r\nTwo distinct cases exist:\r\n\r\n1. **Design decomposition** — approved design/content is missing or too coarse. Identify the smallest missing artifact needed to continue.\r\n2. **Execution decomposition** — design is concrete, but the implementation record still bundles too many responsibilities/validation targets. Split only already-approved responsibilities.\r\n\r\nThe Decomposer must not generate missing design during the same decision that detects the gap.\r\n\r\nDetecting missing design and creating missing design are separate authority events.\r\n\r\n## Artifact Authority\r\n\r\nBefore a proposed design/content artifact may be generated, the Artifact Authority Gate answers:\r\n\r\n1. Is the artifact necessary to progress parent work?\r\n2. Which current GDD requirements or approved artifacts authorize it?\r\n3. Which design decisions may it make?\r\n4. Which areas must it not invent, replace, or contradict?\r\n\r\nPossible outcomes conceptually include:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nAUTHORIZED\r\nREJECTED\r\nNEEDS_HUMAN_REVIEW\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe gate authorizes existence/generation. It does not judge the quality of the generated artifact.\r\n\r\nAfter authorization, Artifact GER and applicable evaluator profiles determine whether the artifact is good enough to promote to trusted input.\r\n\r\n## Assignment 3 Integration\r\n\r\nAssignment 3's crew belongs **inside bounded ticket execution**:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPersistent Work Graph chooses WHAT\r\n        ↓\r\nTask Context\r\n        ↓\r\nPlanner\r\n        ↓\r\nImplementer\r\n        ↓\r\nValidator\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe crew should not reconstruct the global roadmap.\r\n\r\n## Assignment 4 Integration\r\n\r\nAssignment 4 RAG answers:\r\n\r\n> What does the GDD say about this work?\r\n\r\nIt supplies canonical evidence to context building, decomposition, semantic evaluation, and refinement.\r\n\r\nRAG is desired-state/canon retrieval, not repository-state truth.\r\n\r\nMilestone 2 should reuse/wrap this machinery rather than rebuild a second RAG system without need.\r\n\r\n## Assignment 5 Integration\r\n\r\nAssignment 5's goal-oriented lesson is now represented by persistent work state plus progressive decomposition.\r\n\r\nFull gap/reconciliation analysis should not run before every feature.\r\n\r\nUse full reconciliation when justified by events such as:\r\n\r\n- material GDD change;\r\n- milestone completion;\r\n- low/empty backlog;\r\n- significant newly discovered dependency;\r\n- disagreement between repository and work graph;\r\n- explicit human request.\r\n\r\nNormal progress uses the persistent graph.\r\n\r\nAssignment 5's implementation agent may also be reused as a bounded implementer/refiner, as Assignment 6 demonstrated.\r\n\r\n## Assignment 6 / GER Integration\r\n\r\nAssignment 6 proved the central repair-loop concept needed later for production execution:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nImplement / Generate\r\n ↓\r\nEvaluate\r\n ↓\r\nValidation Evidence\r\n ├─ PASS → approved\r\n └─ FAIL → structured feedback → Refiner → re-evaluate\r\n                                      ↓\r\n                               retry to budget\r\n                                      ↓\r\n                               Circuit Breaker\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe camera run established production rules:\r\n\r\n1. Static evaluator PASS is not sufficient for interactive Unity behavior.\r\n2. Runtime observations must re-enter the repair loop as structured evidence.\r\n3. Validation history should be auditable enough to reconstruct what happened.\r\n4. A Refiner that makes no relevant change while failures remain has not made progress.\r\n5. No-op repair attempts count against the repair budget.\r\n6. Circuit Breakers bound retries and escalate instead of looping forever.\r\n7. Evaluator contracts should be task/GDD specific, not merely “does it compile?”\r\n\r\nReference:\r\n\r\n`Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md`\r\n\r\n## Validation Evidence Model\r\n\r\nProduction execution should build an evidence bundle rather than trust one PASS/FAIL source.\r\n\r\nPossible evidence sources include:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nGit / scope validation\r\nStatic checks\r\nUnity compilation\r\nEditMode tests\r\nPlayMode tests\r\nRuntime observations\r\nSimulation/adversarial-agent results (later)\r\nTask/GDD semantic evaluation\r\nArtifact canon/design evaluation\r\nArtifact completeness evaluation\r\nStyle evaluation when applicable\r\nFresh semantic diff review\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot every work item needs every evaluator.\r\n\r\nWork type, source requirements, acceptance criteria, and risk determine which evidence is required.\r\n\r\nFailures should be normalized into structured Refiner input.\r\n\r\n## Assignment 7 / Style Evaluator Integration\r\n\r\nAssignment 7 should not become a parallel autonomous architecture.\r\n\r\nWhen Progressive Decomposition identifies an authorized style-sensitive artifact, Assignment 7 can supply a scored evaluator inside Artifact GER:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nGenerator\r\n ↓\r\nStyle Evaluator\r\n ↓\r\nSCORE + REASON\r\n ↓\r\nRefiner\r\n ↓\r\nStyle Evaluator\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe Style Evaluator judges quality/style of content already authorized to exist.\r\n\r\nIt does not authorize creation of new canon or design content.\r\n\r\nArtifact authority and artifact quality remain separate decisions.\r\n\r\n## Git Model\r\n\r\nAutonomous implementation workers must not develop directly on `main`.\r\n\r\nFor each implementation ticket, Milestone 3 should eventually create a branch and worktree such as:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nbranch: claude/NSC-003-player-movement\r\nworktree: .worktrees/NSC-003/\r\n```\r\n\r\nExpected lifecycle:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nReady → Claimed → In Progress → Validating → PR Ready → Merged → Done\r\n```\r\n\r\n“Done” means merged/integrated evidence supports completion, not merely that a worker says it finished.\r\n\r\nDraft PRs should be opened early so humans can inspect ongoing work.\r\n\r\n## Autonomous Supervisor\r\n\r\nThe supervisor, not the model, owns the eventual continuous loop.\r\n\r\nConceptually:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nwhile game_not_complete:\r\n    ready = taskcontrol.ready()\r\n\r\n    if not ready:\r\n        expand_near_frontier_or_reconcile()\r\n        continue\r\n\r\n    work = choose_safe_ready_work(ready)\r\n\r\n    if work_needs_decomposition(work):\r\n        run_progressive_decomposition(work)\r\n        continue\r\n\r\n    if work.kind == \"artifact\":\r\n        authorize_generate_evaluate_or_escalate(work)\r\n        continue\r\n\r\n    claim(work)\r\n    create_branch_worktree_and_draft_pr(work)\r\n    context = build_compact_context(work)\r\n    result = run_bounded_execution_ger(work, context)\r\n\r\n    if result.needs_human:\r\n        preserve_and_escalate(work)\r\n        continue\r\n\r\n    if validation_and_review_pass(result):\r\n        merge(work)\r\n        mark_complete(work)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis remains target architecture; the supervisor itself is not yet implemented.\r\n\r\n## Safety / Cost Controls\r\n\r\nPer-work limits should eventually include:\r\n\r\n- maximum agent runs;\r\n- maximum repair attempts;\r\n- maximum runtime;\r\n- model/token budget;\r\n- maximum no-progress attempts.\r\n\r\nStop/escalate for:\r\n\r\n- repeated validation failure;\r\n- GDD ambiguity;\r\n- unauthorized design expansion;\r\n- architecture-changing dependencies;\r\n- Unity scene/prefab/shared-resource conflict;\r\n- scope expansion;\r\n- budget exhaustion;\r\n- repeated no-op refinement.\r\n\r\nAutonomous means “continue safe bounded work,” not “spend forever” or “invent whatever is missing.”\r\n\r\n## Parallelism\r\n\r\nDo not start with multiple coding workers.\r\n\r\nFirst make one-ticket execution reliable and restartable.\r\n\r\nLater parallelism must honor exclusive-resource claims and be conservative around Unity scenes, prefabs, ProjectSettings, Input Actions, and shared builder scripts.\r\n\r\n## Near-Term Build Strategy\r\n\r\nMilestone 1 is finished. Do not rebuild it.\r\n\r\nThe current strategy is:\r\n\r\n1. confirm `taskcontrol validate` and `taskcontrol ready` remain truthful;\r\n2. run/review the post-M1 adversarial architecture checkpoint;\r\n3. use one real ready/near-ready No Safe Circle task as the anchor for the next slice;\r\n4. build the smallest targeted task-context path needed for that work;\r\n5. reuse Assignment 4 RAG and existing deterministic reconciliation/scanner capabilities where practical;\r\n6. add Progressive Decomposition only when a near-frontier item actually needs it;\r\n7. create artifact proposals rather than invent missing design;\r\n8. authorize/evaluate generated artifacts before downstream use;\r\n9. add the single-ticket supervisor only after compact task context is reliable;\r\n10. productionize generic GER/Unity validation around real tickets;\r\n11. enable continuous autonomous backlog processing only after single-ticket execution is trustworthy;\r\n12. add parallel workers last.\r\n\r\nA strong current real-task anchor is `NSC-003` Player Movement because it is already ready, bounded, and unlocks multiple later systems.\r\n\r\nThis keeps pipeline development tied to capstone progress.\r\n\r\n## High-Level Build Milestones\r\n\r\n1. **Persistent work artifacts + deterministic `taskcontrol` — COMPLETE**\r\n2. **RAG canon service + deterministic project scanner + compact context builder + Progressive Decomposer + Artifact Authority Gate — NEXT**\r\n3. One-ticket autonomous supervisor with claims + branch/worktree/Draft PR\r\n4. Productionize GER execution + deterministic/Unity/runtime validation + evaluator profiles\r\n5. Continuous scheduling + blocker handling + budgets + GitHub visibility + eventual safe parallelism\r\n\r\nAssignment 6 has already produced a working prototype of Milestone 4's central repair-loop concept, so Milestone 4 is production integration rather than invention from zero.\r\n\r\n## Working Rule\r\n\r\nBuild in small stages.\r\n\r\nDo not try to implement the full autonomous pipeline in one context or coding session.\r\n\r\nEach meaningful session should leave durable repository state/documentation so the next session can resume without the previous chat transcript.\r\n\r\nFrom Milestone 2 onward, infrastructure should increasingly be proven by advancing actual No Safe Circle gameplay rather than becoming a separate project that indefinitely delays the game.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.updated","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"todo_list","items":[{"text":"Read mandatory policy and verify the frozen commit/worktree state","completed":true},{"text":"Read the specified architecture canon while excluding prohibited review outputs","completed":true},{"text":"Trace architecture claims into pipeline implementation, Unity assets/tests, and repository history","completed":true},{"text":"Assess production soundness, moving-GDD behavior, authority boundaries, and throughput","completed":true},{"text":"Produce the evidence-backed verdict and single next slice","completed":true}]}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"alternative_architecture\":{\"description\":\"Reorganize around a thin, single-feature delivery ledger. State: stable requirement IDs/revisions plus Git, small near-frontier contracts, append-only attempt journals, and delivery receipts. Planning: human selects one feature; a planner and Unity scanner validate one contract and its actual paths/GUIDs. Execution: one writable provider in an isolated worktree. Validation: deterministic diff/scope checks, Unity compile, EditMode/PlayMode tests, exact committed-scene inspection, semantic review, and human playtesting. Recovery: preserve branch commits and stage journals, resume from the failed stage, and circuit-break after bounded repairs. Unity integration: serialize only through approved editor/builder operations, retain `.meta` identity, run one host Unity job at a time, and compare canonical asset bytes before/after tests.\",\"needed\":true,\"why_better\":\"This preserves the good safety boundaries but removes global reconciliation, provider parity, artifact generation, GitHub synchronization, and parallel scheduling from the critical path. Requirement-level revisions prevent unrelated GDD edits from invalidating every delivered task, while a task preflight prevents stale Unity paths and GUIDs from entering execution. Most importantly, it produces gameplay evidence before investing further in platform machinery.\"},\"architecture_summary\":\"The core topology is good: bounded workers, Git as integrated truth, deterministic validation, runtime feedback, immutable evidence, and human design/merge authority. The current composition is partially unsound because it lacks an end-to-end writable Unity delivery lane and duplicates mutable project facts across too many stores. An ordinary human-approved scene relocation already left canon, 16 contracts, project requirements, and resource locks pointing at a deleted asset while structural validation still passed.\",\"biggest_uncertainty\":\"No real gameplay task has passed through the current AgentRuntime/TaskExecution architecture. Actual implementation quality, Unity failure rate, repair cost, and end-to-end cycle time remain unmeasured; the camera evidence predates the production execution lane.\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"do_not_build_yet\":[\"Parallel workers, generalized worktree scheduling, or merge queues.\",\"GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization.\",\"Provider fallback or additional provider-comparison/review machinery.\",\"A general Progressive Decomposer and Artifact Authority platform before a real task is blocked by missing design.\",\"Style evaluation or automated artifact generation.\",\"A broad incremental project scanner; add only the Unity/task preflight needed by the next slice.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"observation\":\"The checked-out clean tree is exactly the required frozen commit 9f2485dca1b61360e6d02810adc71e021346496e.\",\"path\":\"/workspace\"},{\"observation\":\"Read-only execution of `taskcontrol validate` passed structurally with 37 active contracts, but autonomous dispatch remained disabled. NSC-023 derived `conformant`; NSC-003 derived `not_delivered`. No Unity tests were executed during this review.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\"},{\"observation\":\"Production ExecutionCrew orchestration, Unity execution, task selection, readiness, dispatch, Git workflow, merging, and provider fallback are explicitly unimplemented.\",\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md\"},{\"observation\":\"Both live provider adapters reject repository writing and approved command execution, so AgentRuntime cannot implement a gameplay task.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md\"},{\"observation\":\"TaskExecution only binds a task identity to one invocation; it explicitly owns no selection, Git, Unity, GER, evidence publication, or completion transition.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskExecution/README.md\"},{\"observation\":\"Commit 484e66a moved the populated authoritative scene and its `.meta` identity to `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`; commit 86af98f added path/GUID safeguards.\",\"path\":\"Git history at 484e66a and 86af98f\"},{\"observation\":\"Sixteen active task contracts still cite the deleted `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` path.\",\"path\":\"Tasks/\"},{\"observation\":\"The GDD still declares the deleted nested scene canonical and the populated `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` non-canonical, despite the later human-approved relocation.\",\"path\":\"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"},{\"observation\":\"Project requirements and the shared scene resource group retain the same obsolete path, so future lock acquisition would not protect the real scene.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml and Pipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml\"},{\"observation\":\"The graph validator checks resource-key consistency but not whether `repo-file`, `unity-scene`, repository-evidence, or GUID targets exist.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/work_graph_validate.py\"},{\"observation\":\"The scene-location smoke test correctly protects uniqueness and GUID 92dbd0a3e6c18e245896a66c5120379d, but only scans active C# for obsolete references; it does not cover canon or task metadata.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/Testing/scene_location_smoke_test.py\"},{\"observation\":\"NSC-023 is reported conformant even though its bound contract still contains stale scene repository evidence; its evidence record separately points at the current scene. The evaluator verifies hashes, gates, and listed surfaces, not factual consistency of repository-evidence prose.\",\"path\":\"Tasks/NSC-023.yaml and Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json\"},{\"observation\":\"Conformance binds the normalized hash of the entire GDD. Any GDD edit stales existing evidence, while only a contract hash/revision change produces `needs_replan`. Conformance surfaces are manually enumerated.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py\"},{\"observation\":\"A passing camera EditMode suite previously invoked the saving production builder and rewrote the canonical tracked scene. The non-saving builder seam and clean runner were created in response.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/Testing/README.md\"},{\"observation\":\"The camera twice passed static evaluation but failed human Unity testing for direction, following, and framing; a later refiner also claimed implementation while making no asset change.\",\"path\":\"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md and Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback000.json\"},{\"observation\":\"Since August 21, reachable history contains roughly 205 commits, only three of which touch Assets; those Asset changes concern test safety and scene centralization rather than a new gameplay feature. The repository has 303 pipeline/task/AI-document files versus 51 tracked Asset files.\",\"path\":\"Git history through 9f2485d\"},{\"observation\":\"NSC-003 is classified as `single_agent` despite spanning Input Actions, pointer projection, locomotion, restriction/reset/suspend interfaces, builder wiring, serialized-scene integration, and unresolved input arbitration. Current PlayerMovement still directly polls `Keyboard.current`.\",\"path\":\"Tasks/NSC-003.yaml and Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerMovement.cs\"},{\"observation\":\"Unity 6000.1.8f1 is pinned and the Input System is installed, but Build Settings contain no scenes and the required Tilemap/AI Navigation packages are not configured yet.\",\"path\":\"ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt, ProjectSettings/EditorBuildSettings.asset, and Packages/manifest.json\"}],\"gdd_iteration_concerns\":[\"The architecture currently treats the whole GDD as one versioned unit. An unrelated wording, balance, or room edit will require revalidation of every task whose evidence binds the previous document hash.\",\"A semantic GDD change can require a new contract, different dependencies, implementation rollback, or cancellation. Returning only `needs_revalidation` against the old contract frames design evolution incorrectly.\",\"There are no stable requirement IDs/revisions in canon and no implemented causal mapping from changed requirements to contracts, code/assets, tests, and downstream obligations.\",\"Reconciliation is correctly immutable, but the reviewed graph-delta/apply process for later changes is not implemented. The scene relocation demonstrates that ordinary repository evolution can bypass synchronization.\",\"Repository/process facts should not be copied into root design canon unless maintained transactionally. Canon currently contradicts Git about the authoritative scene.\",\"The future change flow should classify edits as editorial, tuning, additive, changed, or removed; update only affected contracts; supersede contracts when meaning changes; and preserve unaffected delivery evidence.\"],\"human_intervention_points\":[\"Choose actual product priority; graph order and apparent readiness are not sufficient.\",\"Resolve NSC-003 input arbitration, click-versus-hold semantics, destination replacement/cancellation, arrival/pathing behavior, and restriction ownership before execution.\",\"Approve normative GDD changes and reviewed contract additions, revisions, supersessions, or cancellations.\",\"Inspect scene/prefab references, Inspector assignments, asset imports, and serialized diffs in the Unity Editor.\",\"Run PlayMode checks for game feel, framing, pointer behavior, animation/readability, balance, and Console errors.\",\"Perform Windows build inspection and approve package/build-setting changes.\",\"Review and merge the task branch; automatic merge is not currently justified.\"],\"hypothetical_failure_solutions\":[\"Deep adversarial freezing of provider JSON subtypes and polymorphic containers protects a future hostile/malformed adapter boundary more than an experienced Unity delivery failure.\",\"Cross-provider ArchitectureReview provenance, latest-pointer, and resume support improves review infrastructure but not gameplay throughput.\",\"Provider fallback and cross-provider-equivalent budgeting are future operational concerns.\",\"Parallel worktree claims, GitHub dashboards, merge queues, and continuous scheduling protect a later multi-worker system.\",\"Artifact Authority, generated-design GER, and style evaluation protect future content-generation cases; the current graph contains no initial artifact task and no demonstrated blocking artifact flow.\"],\"missing_components\":[\"A small approved NSC-003 child contract with resolved input behavior.\",\"A writable, bounded Implementer path using one provider and an isolated branch/worktree.\",\"Task-scoped orchestration from contract to implementation result, deterministic diff, validation, repair, and escalation.\",\"A host Unity execution bridge around the existing clean PowerShell runner.\",\"Deterministic task preflight that validates referenced files, canonical scenes, `.meta` GUIDs, Input Action identities, packages, builder ownership, and Build Settings.\",\"Automatic capture of actual changed paths and scope violations from Git rather than provider claims.\",\"A reviewed evidence publisher that binds actual clean Unity XML, commit/tree, changed surfaces, human approval, and integrated commit.\",\"Requirement-level GDD change-impact analysis and deterministic reviewed contract-delta application.\",\"A derived readiness policy based on current conformance and dependency state; it should remain human-dispatched initially.\"],\"next_slice\":{\"deliverables\":[\"Record a human-approved movement micro-brief resolving click/hold input arbitration, destination replacement/cancellation, arrival/pathing, and UI/spell/door click ownership.\",\"Correct the authoritative scene path in canon, affected task/resource metadata, and validation so this drift cannot recur silently.\",\"Supersede or split NSC-003 into a bounded first contract: Input Actions-based pointer projection plus click/hold player movement. Leave restriction/reset/suspend integration as a follow-up if it cannot remain independently testable.\",\"Add only the minimal one-task writable runner needed to invoke one provider in an isolated worktree and capture the real Git diff.\",\"Implement the movement slice in PlayerMovement, Input Actions, the builder, and the authoritative committed scene without regenerating `.meta` identity.\",\"Add isolated component/PlayMode tests plus direct committed-scene conformance checks, run them through the clean Unity host runner, and complete a human feel/input check.\",\"Merge through human review and publish one exact delivery record; use it to prove the first evidence-derived dependency/readiness transition.\"],\"proof_of_value\":\"One approved gameplay contract travels from planned to implemented, cleanly Unity-tested, human-playtested, merged, evidence-published, and currently conformant at HEAD. Measure elapsed time, model invocations, repair count, human minutes, and escaped defects. That is the first credible evidence that the architecture makes development materially faster.\",\"title\":\"NSC-003A — End-to-End Mouse Movement Delivery Lane\",\"why\":\"This is the smallest slice that exercises the actual value chain and unlocks spells and door interaction. If infrastructure additions were forbidden, the first autonomous failure would be immediate: current providers cannot write or execute commands. With an ordinary human-driven coding agent, the first semantic failure would be NSC-003's unresolved input contract; after implementation, Unity execution and evidence publication would still be manual. This slice exposes and closes all three gaps without building the later platform.\"},\"observed_failure_solutions\":[\"Runtime Unity feedback feeding GER solved camera direction, following, and framing defects missed by static semantic review.\",\"The no-op progress guard prevented a refiner's unchanged `implemented` claim from being accepted and charged it against the repair budget.\",\"The non-saving in-memory builder seam separated builder capability from canonical serialized state and stopped tests from saving the production scene.\",\"Direct committed-scene tests, byte comparison, and the clean runner address the experienced destructive passing-test incident.\",\"Moving the scene with its `.meta`, asserting one authoritative scene, and checking the GUID address the duplicate-scene/asset-identity incident.\",\"Immutable reconciliation runs, recovery scripts, bounded retries, and deterministic finding identities address actual max-turn, timeout, interrupted-run, and ordering failures visible in history.\",\"Schema-v2 contracts and committed conformance evidence prevent a mutable task status or worker claim from becoming completion truth, although autonomous dispatch had not yet experienced that failure in production.\",\"Production GDDRAG fixes the demonstrated staleness of the older Assignment 4 index, while correctly not claiming top-k coverage completeness.\"],\"overall_verdict\":\"partially_unsound\",\"overengineering\":[\"The project implemented two live provider adapters and migrated an eight-role architecture-review consumer before enabling one provider to write a gameplay change.\",\"The accepted staged plan requires both adapters and full ExecutionCrew roles before the first real provider-interchangeable task proof; that ordering optimizes abstraction confidence ahead of product throughput.\",\"Global multi-model reconciliation, verification, streaming refinement, recovery, migrations, and immutable histories consumed substantial effort for a 37-contract bootstrap. They should not become the normal response to iterative GDD edits.\",\"There are multiple overlapping architecture/status documents with already-stale milestone claims. Operational status should be generated from code where possible.\",\"The repository's recent commit/file ratio shows infrastructure becoming a second product: extensive pipeline churn has not produced a post-camera gameplay feature.\",\"Provider trust-boundary hardening is technically strong, but much of its depth has lower current expected value than a writable task lane, Unity preflight, and one real gameplay delivery.\"],\"state_and_authority_concerns\":[\"Necessary boundaries: approved GDD/feature decisions define intent; task contracts define bounded work and gates; Git defines integrated code/assets; attempt journals define transient execution; evidence receipts plus current Git derive conformance; humans own ambiguous design, visual/feel approval, and merge authority.\",\"Necessary separation: generic AgentRuntime must not own NSC task identity, and TaskExecution audit artifacts must not become completion evidence. The ADR-039 direction is correct.\",\"Duplicated responsibility: authoritative scene paths and other repository facts appear in GDD prose, task repository evidence, exclusive-resource keys, project requirements, RAG chunks, current-state documents, and conformance surfaces.\",\"The living graph is called operational state, but schema v2 intentionally contains no operational status and readiness is disabled. It is currently a contract/dependency catalog, not an operational work graph.\",\"Manual conformance-surface selection can under-approximate Unity dependencies. A package, Input Action, prefab, ProjectSetting, referenced ScriptableObject, or builder dependency omitted from the receipt can change without invalidating conformance.\",\"Reconciliation history should remain audit history, but it should not be a prerequisite authority layer for routine local changes. A requirement/task delta plus human approval is enough.\",\"GitHub should remain a projection/dashboard if introduced; it must not duplicate contract, evidence, or conformance authority.\"],\"strong_decisions\":[\"One bounded worker and human merge authority before parallelism are appropriate for Unity's shared serialized assets.\",\"Workers and provider adapters produce claims, never test, merge, readiness, or completion truth.\",\"Task contracts are separated from mutable completion status, and committed Git objects—not a dirty working copy—drive conformance evaluation.\",\"Exact commit/tree, artifact blob, task revision, canon hash, and human approval binding make evidence auditable.\",\"Unity tests must start and finish with a clean tree, parse XML, preserve logs, and report exact Unity version and limitations.\",\"Builder output and committed serialized artifact conformance are treated as separate claims.\",\"Scenes and prefabs move with `.meta` files; duplicate authoritative scenes are prohibited.\",\"Runtime and visual evidence can override a static evaluator pass and return structured feedback to bounded repair.\",\"Missing design is escalated rather than silently invented.\",\"Parallelism, automatic merge, and autonomous dispatch remain disabled until a one-ticket lane is trustworthy.\"],\"structural_flaws\":[\"There is no end-to-end state machine connecting approved plan → writable execution → Git-observed changes → Unity validation → repair → human review → merge → delivery evidence → dependency readiness.\",\"Moving canon is modeled as whole-document invalidation, not requirement-level versioning and impact. This will generate broad revalidation work while still failing to revise contracts whose meaning changed.\",\"Unity asset authority is duplicated and already contradictory after one routine human-approved relocation. Structural validation passes because it verifies key consistency rather than target existence and GUID identity.\",\"The current graph can label an item `single_agent` without resolving gameplay choices or proving its Unity integration surface is bounded; NSC-003 is the concrete counterexample.\",\"A conformance record can be current while descriptive repository evidence inside its bound contract is factually stale, because only hashes, declared gates, and manually selected surfaces are evaluated.\",\"The production runtime deliberately cannot write or execute approved commands, and the Unity runner remains an external manual operation. Therefore the current architecture is an audit/review platform, not an autonomous development pipeline.\",\"The milestone ordering puts compact context, decomposition, provider parity, and generalized crew infrastructure ahead of the shortest working gameplay loop, despite the stated real-slice rule.\",\"Worktree isolation alone does not solve Unity production integration. Each candidate still needs a viable Unity project/library strategy, serialized asset inspection, exclusive host execution, and post-rebase validation.\"],\"throughput_assessment\":\"Major near-term leverage is not yet demonstrated. The architecture has materially improved safety, repeatability, and auditability, especially around Unity tests and camera validation. But at the frozen commit, zero tasks are dispatchable, providers cannot edit, NSC-003 is not safely specified, Unity validation is external, and evidence publication is manual. Recent history is overwhelmingly pipeline work with no new gameplay feature. The system is therefore slower than direct expert-assisted development today; it becomes plausibly high-leverage only after the proposed vertical slice proves a repeatable one-ticket cycle.\",\"verdict_reason\":\"The foundational production instincts are strong, so this is not a fundamentally wrong approach. It is partially unsound because moving-design synchronization, Unity asset authority, and the execution-to-evidence path are either incorrectly framed or absent. The existing stale-scene contradiction is direct evidence that the current stores do not stay coherent, and the lack of a writable Unity delivery lane means the architecture cannot yet achieve its stated days-instead-of-weeks goal.\"}"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"todo_list","items":[{"text":"Read mandatory policy and verify the frozen commit/worktree state","completed":true},{"text":"Read the specified architecture canon while excluding prohibited review outputs","completed":true},{"text":"Trace architecture claims into pipeline implementation, Unity assets/tests, and repository history","completed":true},{"text":"Assess production soundness, moving-GDD behavior, authority boundaries, and throughput","completed":true},{"text":"Produce the evidence-backed verdict and single next slice","completed":true}]}}
